From 207aaa4e041347b9ef15baaf71c77ab93d6c6bac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:59:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 112/113] dynarmic: link sites in one compact list per target
 (48-byte flat map slots, not 232)

PatchInformation held four small_vector<CodePtr, 4> (224 bytes), in a boost flat map that costs
every slot, used or not, its full size: one core's map was 57 MB in Zelda: Echoes of Wisdom
(about 215,000 link targets), a single allocation, and the next growth would need 114 MB more.
That 54.6 MiB allocation, needing a new overflow heap on the PS4, is where two runs aborted.
Now one small_vector<u64, 2> of sites, each with its kind (jg, jz, jmp, mov rcx) in its top two
bits. Patching order within a target doesn't matter (each site independent).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
